                    <death when="1808-02-13"/>
                    <occupation>MP, soldier and colonial governor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> It is probable that it is this Fullarton whom Godwin records as being at
                            Gibbon's birthday party. </p>
                        <p> Ed Pope adds: At Gibbon's birthday party (where Godwin probably wasn't),
                            this was perhaps William Fullarton (DNB 1754-1808) then MP for
                            Haddington. The writing suggests an 'r' though the ink is hardly
                            visible.</p> <p> SOCIETY
                            FOR CONSTITUTIONAL INFORMATION: Col Fullarton of St James St proposed
                            24.6.1791 by Count Zenobio 2nded John Frost See DNB article William
                            Fullarton 1754-1808</p>
                    </note>
